.\" Man page for ferngeist-gateway.
.\" Keep in sync with cmd/ferngeist/main.go.
.TH FERNGEIST-GATEWAY 1 "2026-10-20" "ferngeist-gateway" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ferngeist\-gateway \- manage the Ferngeist gateway daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ferngeist\-gateway
.RI [ global\-options ]
.I command
.RI [ command\-options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Ferngeist Gateway
is a self\-hosted backend service for ACP\-compatible coding agents. It runs a
local daemon that discovers and launches agents, exposes an HTTP and WebSocket
API to paired clients, and can provision remote access.
.PP
This manual describes the command\-line interface. The daemon is normally
installed as a per\-user background service with
.B daemon install
and then controlled with the other
.B daemon
subcommands.
.PP
Commands that read or change daemon state
.RB ( pair ,
.BR devices ,
.BR agents )
talk to the running daemon over its local admin API. When the daemon does not
answer, they exit with status 2 so scripts can tell
\(lqstart the daemon\(rq
apart from an ordinary command failure.
.SH OPTIONS
.SS Global options
.TP
.BR \-\-version ", " \-v
Print version information and exit. The output lists the version, commit,
build time, and Go version.
.TP
.BR \-\-help ", " \-h
Print help for the command and exit.
.SH COMMANDS
.SS update
.B ferngeist\-gateway update
.PP
Check for and install the latest stable gateway release. The downloaded
binary is verified against the release's
.B SHA256SUMS
before it replaces the running one.
.PP
Only self\-managed installs self\-update. Builds installed from Homebrew,
apt, dnf/yum, pacman, or winget refuse and must be updated with the package
manager instead.
.SS daemon
.B ferngeist\-gateway daemon
.I command
.PP
Run and manage the gateway daemon. With no subcommand, the list of daemon
subcommands is printed.
.SS "daemon run"
.B ferngeist\-gateway daemon run
.RI [ options ]
.PP
Run the gateway daemon in the foreground. The process serves the public API
and the local admin API until it receives an interrupt signal or its binary
is replaced during an upgrade.
.TP
.B \-\-lan
Expose the gateway on the local network. This enables LAN discovery and
access and, unless a listen address is already configured, listens on
.IR 0.0.0.0:5788 .
.TP
.B \-\-remote
Provision remote access over Tailscale, using the Tailscale CLI when it is
available and the embedded node otherwise.
.TP
.BI \-\-listen\-addr " address"
Override the public API listen address for this run.
.TP
.BI \-\-public\-base\-url " url"
Advertise a public gateway URL for pairing.
.SS "daemon install"
.B ferngeist\-gateway daemon install
.RI [ options ]
.PP
Install and start the daemon as a per\-user service. On Linux this writes a
systemd user unit, on macOS a LaunchAgent, and on Windows a per\-user scheduled
task. No administrator privileges are required.
.TP
.B \-\-lan
Listen on
.I 0.0.0.0
and enable LAN access. The default is localhost\-only.
.TP
.B \-\-remote
Provision remote access over Tailscale as with
.BR "daemon run \-\-remote" .
.TP
.BI \-\-host " host"
Host interface for the daemon listen address. Optional; defaults to
.IR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.BI \-\-port " port"
Port for the daemon listen address. Optional; defaults to 5788.
.TP
.BI \-\-public\-url " url"
Public base URL announced to clients. Optional.
.TP
.B \-\-keep\-settings
Reuse the settings of the existing install. The other flags then only apply
to a first install. Package upgrades use this.
.SS "daemon uninstall"
.B ferngeist\-gateway daemon uninstall
.RI [ options ]
.PP
Stop the daemon and remove its background\-service registration. Installed
files, configuration, and data are left in place unless
.B \-\-purge
is given.
.TP
.B \-\-purge
Also remove daemon data, logs, and managed binaries.
.SS "daemon start"
.B ferngeist\-gateway daemon start
.PP
Start the installed daemon user service.
.SS "daemon stop"
.B ferngeist\-gateway daemon stop
.PP
Stop the installed daemon user service.
.SS "daemon restart"
.B ferngeist\-gateway daemon restart
.PP
Restart the installed daemon user service.
.SS "daemon status"
.B ferngeist\-gateway daemon status
.PP
Show the daemon service state and whether its API is reachable.
.SS pair
.B ferngeist\-gateway pair
.PP
Start an interactive pairing flow. The command prints the pairing code, its
expiry, a scannable QR code, the pairing payload, and the target URL, then
waits for Ferngeist Android to complete the pairing. Press Ctrl\-C to cancel.
.PP
A running daemon is required.
.SS devices
.B ferngeist\-gateway devices
.I command
.PP
Manage paired devices. A running daemon is required.
.SS "devices list"
.B ferngeist\-gateway devices list
.PP
List paired devices with their device ID, device name, and credential
expiry time.
.SS "devices revoke"
.B ferngeist\-gateway devices revoke
.I device\-id
.PP
Revoke one paired device and invalidate its credential immediately.
.SS agents
.B ferngeist\-gateway agents
.I command
.PP
Manage custom ACP agents. Custom agents are registered with the daemon and
then list and start like agents from the built\-in catalog. A running daemon
is required.
.SS "agents add"
.B ferngeist\-gateway agents add
.BI \-\-name " name"
.BI \-\-command " command"
.RB [ \-\-args " arg " ]...
.RB [ \-\-hint " text " ]
.PP
Register a custom agent. The display name is required; the agent ID is
derived from it as
.IR custom\-<slug> .
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name"
Display name for the agent.
.TP
.BI \-\-command " command"
Bare PATH executable name or absolute path to the agent binary.
.TP
.BI \-\-args " arg"
One argument for the agent command. Repeat the flag for multiple arguments.
.TP
.BI \-\-hint " text"
Optional note shown to clients.
.SS "agents list"
.B ferngeist\-gateway agents list
.PP
List all agents, including embedded, registry, and custom agents.
.SS "agents update"
.B ferngeist\-gateway agents update
.I agent\-id
.RB [ \-\-name " name " ]
.RB [ \-\-command " command " ]
.RB [ \-\-args " arg " ]...
.RB [ \-\-clear\-args ]
.RB [ \-\-hint " text " ]
.PP
Edit a custom agent. Only the supplied fields change; the agent ID cannot
change.
.TP
.BI \-\-name " name"
New display name.
.TP
.BI \-\-command " command"
New bare PATH executable name or absolute path.
.TP
.BI \-\-args " arg"
Replacement argument. Repeat the flag for multiple arguments. Cannot be
combined with
.BR \-\-clear\-args .
.TP
.B \-\-clear\-args
Clear the argument list.
.TP
.BI \-\-hint " text"
New hint. An empty string clears it.
.SS "agents rm"
.B ferngeist\-gateway agents rm
.I agent\-id
.PP
Remove a custom agent. The ID is the
.I custom\-<slug>
identifier shown by
.BR "agents list" .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
The daemon is configured through environment variables. The most commonly
used are:
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LISTEN_ADDR
Public API listen address. Defaults to
.IR 127.0.0.1:5788 .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_ADMIN_ADDR
Local admin API listen address. Defaults to
.IR 127.0.0.1:5789 .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_ENABLE_LAN
Enable LAN discovery and access. Set to
.I 1
to enable.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_PUBLIC_BASE_URL
Public URL clients use to reach the gateway.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_STATE_DB
SQLite state database path. Platform\-dependent.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LOG_DIR
Log directory. Platform\-dependent.
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LOG_LEVEL
Log level:
.IR debug ,
.IR info ,
.IR warn ,
or
.IR error .
Defaults to
.IR info .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_JS_RUNTIME
Runtime used to launch npm\-distributed registry agents:
.IR auto
(bun when it is on
.IR PATH ,
else node),
.IR bun ,
.IR node ,
or
.IR npm .
Defaults to
.IR auto .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_TAILSCALE_MODE
Remote access provisioning:
.IR off ,
.IR auto ,
.IR cli ,
or
.IR tsnet .
Defaults to
.IR off .
.TP
.B FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_UPDATE_CHECK_ENABLED
Check GitHub Releases for a newer stable version. Set to
.I 0
or
.I false
to disable.
.PP
The complete list, with defaults and platform notes, is documented in
.BR ferngeist\-gateway\-env (1).
The project repository also carries
.I docs/configuration.md
with additional context.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_STATE_DB
Paired devices, settings, and runtime state. The default path is
platform\-dependent.
.TP
.I $FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_LOG_DIR
Daemon and agent logs. The default path is platform\-dependent.
.TP
.I $FERNGEIST_GATEWAY_MANAGED_BIN_DIR
Installed agent binaries and npm agent installs. The default path is
platform\-dependent.
.TP
.I /usr/share/doc/ferngeist\-gateway/README.md
Package documentation.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
Success.
.TP
.B 1
The command failed. The reason is printed to standard error.
.TP
.B 2
The daemon did not answer. Start it with
.B ferngeist\-gateway daemon start
or
.BR "daemon install" .
.TP
.B 75
The daemon stopped because its binary was replaced during an upgrade. This is
the
.B EX_TEMPFAIL
status; restart the daemon.
.SH NOTES
The gateway runs as the same operating\-system user as the daemon. Pairing a
device therefore grants that device the same access to the project directories
the agents can read and modify.
.SH BUGS
Report bugs at
.IR https://github.com/arafatamim/ferngeist\-acp\-gateway/issues .
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR ferngeist\-gateway\-env (1),
and the project documentation in the source repository:
.IR docs/api.md ,
.IR docs/configuration.md ,
.IR docs/install.md ,
and
.IR docs/usage.md .
.PP
.IR https://github.com/arafatamim/ferngeist\-acp\-gateway .
